  "findings": [
    "Equal single-invocation DXC cost does not establish equal runtime compile counts, timing or critical-path placement.",
    "Native D3D12 shader creation consumes existing bytecode. The Web backend creates a WGSL module; browser DXC happens later and is outside UE ShaderCompileWorker/ShaderMap completion.",
    "Editor material fallback and ODSC are separate from runtime PSO creation. They do not automatically provide a fallback for a browser PSO whose UE ShaderMap is already complete.",
    "Normal asynchronous PSOs still register a completion dependency. Current Web path waits before command-list translation to avoid owner-thread callback self-wait.",
    "Current local UE5.8 explicitly disables PSO precaching for WITH_EDITOR; component readiness/proxy-delay logic also excludes GIsEditor.",
    "UE5 reduces work or moves it earlier and can defer visibility or use fallback. It does not universally eliminate first-use PSO stalls."
  ],
